but inherently\par   platform-specific -- opening a default browser -- and allow programmers (you,\par   for example) to do so without worrying about dropping into native code or\par   doing anything else similarly evil.\par   \par   Anyway, this code is completely in Java and will run on all JDK 1.1-compliant\par   systems without modification or a need for additional libraries. All classes\par   that are required on certain platforms to allow this to run are dynamically\par   loaded at runtime via reflection and, if not found, will not cause this to do\par   anything other than returning an error when opening the browser.\par   \par   There are certain system requirements for this class, as it's running through\par   Runtime.exec(), which is Java's way of making a native system call.\par   Currently, this requires that a Macintosh have a Finder which supports the\par   GURL event, which is true for Mac OS 8.0 and 8.1 systems that have the\par   Internet Scripting AppleScript dictionary installed in the Scripting\par   Additions folder in the Extensions folder (which is installed by default as\par   far as I know under Mac OS 8.0 and 8.1), and for all Mac OS 8.5 and later\par   systems. On Windows, it only runs under Win32 systems (NT, 4.0, \par   as well as later versions of all). On other systems, this drops back\par   from the inherently platform-sensitive concept of a default browser and\par   simply attempts to launch Netscape via a shell command.\par   \par   This code is Copyright 1999-2001 by Eric Albert (ejalbert@cs.stanford.edu)\par   and may be redistributed or modified in any form without restrictions as long\par   as the portion of this comment from this paragraph through the end of the\par   comment is not removed. The author requests that he be notified of any\par   application, applet, or other binary that makes use of this code, but that's\par   more out of curiosity than anything and is not required. This software\par   includes no warranty. The a